# General Rules

## Before writing any code
1. Read `docs/PRD.md` to understand the product
2. Read `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` for codebase structure
3. Read `docs/RULES.md` for all coding standards
4. Search for existing implementations before creating new ones

## Key Architecture
- `src/app/**/page.tsx` — thin entry points only, import from features/
- `src/features/<domain>/` — all domain logic
- `src/services/*.service.ts` — all Supabase/API calls
- `src/components/ui/` — reusable UI primitives
- `src/types/index.ts` — all domain types

## TypeScript
- Never use `any`
- Use `import type { ... }` for type-only imports
- All exported components must have typed props

## Security
- Never put secrets in client code
- Always verify auth in Server Actions
- Never trust client-sent user IDs

## Testing
- Run `npm test` after every task
- Run `npm run build` before marking done
